on of David\"). That is the legal father by the house. It is not the begetting. The defender's Numbers 1:2 and 1:18 reckon \"by the house of their fathers,\" a register of houses. They do not state seed.\n\n## 9. The sign\n\n[L1] Isaiah 7:14: \"Behold, a virgin shall conceive, and bear a son.\"\n[L1] Matthew 1:23: \"Behold, a virgin shall be with child, and shall bring forth a son.\"\n[L2] parthenos (G3933), \"a virgin,\" stands in Matthew 1:23, and again in Luke 1:27.\n[L4] The prophecy is cited as fulfilled in \"all this\" (Matthew 1:22), and the fulfilment is a virgin with child. A father's seed would erase the sign. The defender gives no row that answers Matthew 1:23.\n\n---\n\n## DECLARED CHAIN (Challenger)\n\n**C1.** The begetting in Mary is of the Holy Ghost, not of Joseph. [L1] Matthew 1:20 \"for that which is conceived in her is of the Holy Ghost. [conceived: Gr. begotten]\" [L2] gennao (G1080), \"to procreate,\" and ek (G1537), \"out of, origin\" [L3] Matthew 1:18 \"found with child of the Holy Ghost\" [L4] the father-verb has the Holy Ghost as its origin.\n\n**C2.** Matthew's line breaks at Joseph. [L1] Matthew 1:16 \"Jacob begat Joseph the husband of Mary, of whom was born Jesus\" [L2] egennesen \"begat\" gives way to egennethe \"was born,\" and hes \"of whom\" is feminine [L3] Matthew 1:2 \"Abraham begat Isaac\" [L4] Joseph is husband of Mary, and the born child is of her.\n\n**C3.** \"Son of Joseph\" is the supposed title. [L1] Luke 3:23 \"being (as was supposed) the son of Joseph\" [L2] nomizo (G3543), \"to suppose\" [L3] Luke 2:49 \"my Father's business\" [L4] the named-father rows are reputed and household use, corrected by the child's own word.\n\n**C4.** The conception was before any coming together, and Joseph did not know her until the birth. [L1] Matthew 1:25 \"And knew her not till she had brought forth her firstborn son\" [L2] ginosko (G1097), \"to know,\" and synerchomai (G4905) [L3] Matthew 1:18 \"before they came together, she was found wi