his be, seeing I know not a man?\" | PROVEN IN [DR1]\nLuke 1:34 \"Then said Mary unto the angel, How shall this be, seeing I know not a man?\" -- MEANS: the question asks how, and the answer that follows supplies the Holy Ghost and the power of the Highest -- [L2] aner (G435) (a man) | [L3] Luke 1:27 \"To a virgin espoused to a man whose name was Joseph, of the house of David; and the virgin's name [was] Mary.\" | PROVEN IN [DR1]\n1 Chronicles 28:6 \"And he said unto me, Solomon thy son, he shall build my house and my courts: for I have chosen him [to be] my son, and I will be his father.\" -- MEANS: Solomon's sonship rests on a choosing, whereas the sonship in Luke 1:35 is joined by \"therefore\" to the conception -- [L2] bachar (H977) (to select, to choose) | [L3] Luke 1:35 \"And the angel answered and said unto her, The Holy Ghost shall come upon thee, and the power of the Highest shall overshadow thee: therefore also that holy thing which shall be born of thee shall be called the Son of God.\" | PROVEN IN [DR1]\n\n6. LINK 2: The defender's reading of Mary's word in Luke 2:48.\n\"It fits D2: Mary's word is household fact, kept by the same hand that wrote supposed.\"\nSTEP: Mary's \"thy father\" settles that Joseph is the father -- ASSUMES: that \"father\" in Luke 2:48 means the begetter -- ROWS GIVE: Luke 1:32 \"He shall be great, and shall be called the Son of the Highest: and the Lord God shall give unto him the throne of his father David:\"\nPRESSED WITH:\nLuke 3:23 \"And Jesus himself began to be about thirty years of age, being (as was supposed) the son of Joseph, which was [the son] of Heli,\" -- MEANS: the narrator marks \"son of Joseph\" as what was supposed or customary, the sense the defender's own Acts 16:13 gives to \"wont\" -- [L2] nomizo (G3543) (to suppose, to be wont) | [L3] Acts 16:13 \"And on the sabbath we went out of the city by a river side, where prayer was wont to be made; and we sat down, and spake unto the women which resorted [thither].\