tands in \"hast thou prepared\", and the margin reads \"thou hast fitted me\".\n[L3] Galatians 4:4: \"God sent forth his Son, made of a woman\". Hebrews 2:14: \"he also himself likewise took part of the same\", that is, flesh and blood. Hebrews 2:17: \"in all things it behoved him to be made like unto [his] brethren\".\n[L4] The body is prepared by God (Hebrews 10:5) and made of a woman (Galatians 4:4). It is real flesh and blood, shared in full with his brethren (Hebrews 2:14, Hebrews 2:17). I hold the preparation and the flesh together.\n\n## Where the position stands\n\n[L1] Matthew 1:18 dates the finding: \"When as his mother Mary was espoused to Joseph, before they came together, she was found with child of the Holy Ghost.\" Matthew 1:25 dates Joseph's not knowing: \"And knew her not till she had brought forth her firstborn son.\"\n[L2] synerchomai (G4905), meaning \"cohabit (conjugally)\", stands in \"came together\" in Matthew 1:18. ginosko (G1097) stands in \"knew her not\" in Matthew 1:25.\n[L3] Matthew 1:22 and Matthew 1:23 say it was done to fulfil what was spoken: \"Behold, a virgin shall be with child, and shall bring forth a son\". Matthew 1:21 and Luke 1:13 give Joseph the naming: \"thou shalt call his name JESUS\". Matthew 1:25 records it done: \"he called his name JESUS\".\n[L4] The child is found in Mary before the coming together (Matthew 1:18). Joseph knew her not until she brought forth (Matthew 1:25). The stated source is the Holy Ghost (Matthew 1:20), and the sign spoken is a virgin with child (Matthew 1:23). Joseph is the husband who takes Mary and names the child (Matthew 1:24, Matthew 1:25). The record gives Christ a human mother, Mary, and a house in David, but no biological human father. That is the standard reading, and it stands on the rows above.\n\n[ANTI-CHEAT CHECK -- computed by the system's enforcer, not by a judge (a TRIAL check): this close round reverses the same side's own earlier reading of Luke 1:13. The close says: \"Matthew